"Places scheduled activities against calendar time so that duration, overlap, milestones and approved changes are visible.\n\nUse when: Coordinate time-bound work with explicit dates. Compare a current project schedule with an approved baseline.\n\nAvoid when: The team has only broad uncertainty horizons or needs scope decomposition first.\n\nVisual grammar: Horizontal bars span scheduled start and finish dates. Task rows may group related work; milestone marks denote zero-duration events. Optional dependency links retain declared relationship types.\n\nBuild: Define activities and a common calendar with working-time assumptions. Determine dependencies and resource-feasible start and finish dates. Add only useful milestones and distinguish baseline, actual and forecast information.\n\nCheck: Bar lengths match the stated calendar and duration convention. Milestones have no artificial duration. Dependencies and resource assumptions support the displayed dates.\n\nPitfalls: Drawing attractive bars before checking schedule feasibility. Treating percent complete as a reliable forecast of remaining effort.\n\nExample: A venue refurbishment schedules permits, construction, inspections and reopening, showing overlapping work and a clearly distinguished approved baseline.\n\nAlternatives: Activity network, Milestone roadmap."
